In a longitudinal data collection scenario, clients report their binary data changes at specific time intervals, and a server aggregates these reports to estimate the marginal changes over time. Given the length of the time horizon (`d`), the number of changes in the differential vector (`k`), and the privacy parameter (`eps`), what are the marginal estimates of the longitudinal data?

