In a scenario where there are several husband-wife pairs and a boat that can carry a limited number of people, how can all pairs safely cross a river if each wife is jealous and will not stay with another man without her husband present? Given the number of pairs and the capacity of the boat, what is the sequence of moves required to ensure all pairs reach the other side of the river without any wife being left alone with another man?

The input and output requirements are as follows:

